1. Purpose

Mail-Bridge is distributed under a source-available licensing model designed to:

* Allow individuals and organizations to self-host and use the software.
* Protect the commercial value of the project.
* Prevent unauthorized SaaS reselling, hosting, cloning, or competitive commercialization.
* Encourage community contributions while preserving sustainability for the maintainers.

This license is inspired by the principles of the Business Source License (BUSL) model while being customized specifically for Mail-Bridge.

2. Definitions

For the purposes of this License:

2.1 “Licensor”

Means the copyright owner(s), maintainers, or contributors authorized to distribute Mail-Bridge.

2.2 “Licensed Work”

Means the Mail-Bridge software, including:

* Source code
* APIs
* Containers
* Build scripts
* Infrastructure templates
* Documentation
* User interfaces
* Plugins officially distributed by the Licensor
* Any derivative works distributed under this License

2.3 “Production Use”

Means any use of the Licensed Work in an environment that:

* Serves real users,
* Sends actual email traffic,
* Supports commercial operations,
* Is used internally by an organization,
* Is used for testing commercial workflows,
* Is accessible outside a single developer machine.

2.4 “Commercial Offering”

Means providing the Licensed Work or derivative functionality:

* As a hosted service,
* As a managed service,
* As a multi-tenant platform,
* As a white-labeled solution,
* As a commercial email platform,
* As an API product,
* As a SaaS/PaaS offering,
* As part of a paid enterprise solution,
* Or in any product where Mail-Bridge functionality is monetized.

2.5 “Change Date”

Means the date on which the Licensed Work automatically converts to the Change License described in Section 13.

2.6 “Open Source Components”

Means third-party dependencies that are separately licensed under their own licenses.

3. Grant of Rights

Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, the Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

* View the source code,
* Download and build the software,
* Modify the Licensed Work,
* Self-host the Licensed Work,
* Use the Licensed Work internally,
* Deploy the Licensed Work for personal or organizational use,
* Create internal customizations,
* Submit contributions to the project.

These rights are granted only if you fully comply with this License.

4. Allowed Usage

The following uses are explicitly permitted:

4.1 Personal Self-Hosting

Individuals may self-host Mail-Bridge for personal or non-commercial usage.

4.2 Internal Organizational Usage

Organizations may self-host Mail-Bridge internally for their own operational email workflows.

Examples include:

* Transactional email systems
* Marketing email systems
* Internal notification infrastructure
* Multi-provider routing
* SMTP orchestration
* SES/SendGrid/Postmark/Mailgun integrations
* Internal automation systems

4.3 Internal Modifications

You may modify the Licensed Work for internal usage.

4.4 Development and Testing

You may use the Licensed Work in staging, testing, CI/CD, QA, development, and non-production environments.

5. Restrictions

Unless explicitly authorized in writing by the Licensor, you MAY NOT:

5.1 Offer Mail-Bridge as a Hosted Service

You may not:

* Sell hosted Mail-Bridge instances,
* Operate a public Mail-Bridge cloud,
* Provide Mail-Bridge as a SaaS platform,
* Offer managed Mail-Bridge deployments,
* Provide Mail-Bridge functionality as an API business,
* Resell Mail-Bridge access commercially.

5.2 Compete Commercially

You may not use Mail-Bridge or derivative works to build or operate a competing commercial product.

This includes:

* Commercial email delivery platforms,
* Multi-tenant email SaaS products,
* Email infrastructure orchestration services,
* Bulk email management platforms,
* Hosted SMTP routing products,
* White-labeled email systems.

5.3 Remove Notices

You may not remove or alter:

* Copyright notices,
* Attribution notices,
* License notices,
* Branding references where required,
* Legal headers.

5.4 Misrepresentation

You may not falsely claim:

* Ownership of the Licensed Work,
* Original authorship,
* Official partnership,
* Certification,
* Sponsorship by the Licensor.

5.5 Trademark Usage

This License does not grant trademark rights.

You may not use the “Mail-Bridge” name, logo, branding, or related identifiers in a way that implies endorsement or official association without written permission.

5.6 License Circumvention

You may not attempt to bypass:

* License restrictions,
* Usage controls,
* Deployment limitations,
* Commercial restrictions,
* Feature enforcement systems.

6. Source Code Distribution

You may distribute modified or unmodified versions of the Licensed Work only if:

* The distribution remains under this License,
* All copyright notices are retained,
* All license files are retained,
* The recipient receives a copy of this License,
* You clearly document modifications,
